WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.120
Right from the beginning of the One Piece
Saga, we are being told that the Marines are

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.760
the greatest enemies for pirates and a massive
obstacle for Luffy becoming pirate king.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.860
To put it simply, being a marine and being
a pirate are as opposite as it gets in One

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.860
Piece.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.400
Pirates want absolute freedom and change,
while Marines want control and stability.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.731
And so Luffy’s path to becoming a legendary
pirate, is full of battles with the Marine

00:00:18.731 --> 00:00:19.731
organization.

00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:23.789
However, during the mini arc about Luffy’s
childhood, it’s actually explained that

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:28.340
his grandfather, who raised him instead of
his parents and who is one of the most powerful

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.580
and famous Marines in the story, always wanted
Luffy to follow in his footsteps.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:37.340
Now, in the end, Luffy of course chose to
follow in the footsteps of Shanks instead,

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.590
quickly becoming a pirate and a prime target
for the Marines.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:45.110
But that leaves a very interesting question
on the table: What if Luffy never got inspired

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.110
by Shanks?

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:50.160
What if instead of a pirate, Luffy had become
a Marine?

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.181
So our story starts during Luffy’s childhood,
where he originally got inspired to become

00:00:54.181 --> 00:00:55.181
a pirate.

00:00:55.181 --> 00:01:00.980
Of course, we could simply assume that Luffy
never meets Shanks, however I think we still

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.839
want Luffy to eat his devil fruit, that Shanks
brought with him.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:10.580
So instead, Luffy needs someone else to be
inspired by BEFORE Shanks ever arrives on

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.690
his island.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:15.850
So for our specific scenario here I want to
assume that Luffy’s Grandfather Garp brings

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.119
along one of his former students to visit
Luffy.

00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:23.450
The marine admiral Aokiji.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.560
In the actually story line, Aokiji has always
been sympathetic towards Luffy.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.920
He was relived that Luffy took in Robin and
allowed Luffy and the straw hats to escape

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.830
multiple times.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.560
Throughout the story we are being told that
Aokiji is basically the ideal Marine, who

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.840
has a fair sense of justice and truly cares
about the safety and happiness of the people.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:44.840
Just like Shanks, he is extremely charismatic
and powerful.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.420
So Luffy, who badly needs a role model, sees
him using his epic ice powers and beat up

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.330
some bad guys, which would be a great alternative
to Shanks.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:58.369
Saying goodbye to Luffy’s grandfather Garp,
Aokiji makes Luffy promise to one day become

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:00.240
a great Marine too.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.219
And so Luffy’s new goal is not to become
pirate king.

00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:07.250
Instead, he now wants to become the marine
fleet admiral.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.930
And with that we have the decisive change
in Luffy’s story.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:16.370
Now the rest of his childhood can stay pretty
much exactly the same, training and with Garp,

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.760
Sabo and Ace.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.680
Shanks still arrives at the island.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.989
Luffy still befriends his entire crew.

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:27.500
And he still eats his devil fruit because
he is hungry.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.099
Okay, so before we can talk about what happens
with the other straw hats and how the story

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:36.810
overall plays out from here, i need to make
2 assumptions about the main story line that

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:42.050
are very likely, but not officially confirmed
yet.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.750
Assumption 1: Garp is a member of sword.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.560
Sword is a secret group within the marines
that doesn’t like how the Marines are being

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:56.190
controlled and used by the corrupt world government
of the one piece world.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:01.470
And Assumption 2 is that Shanks knows that
Luffy is important to change the world, and

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:05.560
wants him to become pirate king and find the
one piece.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.360
If you are caught up to the manga, or don’t
mind about spoilers I have videos about both

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.530
these claims, that you can watch later.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:18.451
For us, it’s only important to know, that
Shanks really tries to inspire Luffy to become

00:03:18.451 --> 00:03:20.629
a pirate, but fails.

00:03:20.629 --> 00:03:26.000
And even though Luffy wants to become a Marine,
thanks to Shanks, he still very much likes

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.420
the idea of having a sort of crew or team.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:34.860
So, 10 years later, Luffy sets out in his
small boat in exactly the same way as he does

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.890
in the main timeline.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:42.379
His goal is not to find a pirate crew, but
instead find a marine base where he can join.

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:47.000
He’s still Luffy and has no experience of
sailing a boat.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.409
So once again he ends up in the barrel on
Alvida’s ship.

00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:55.070
There he saves Koby and the two of them end
up in the same town as before.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:04:00.110
This time not to recruit Zoro, but to join
the marines at the base.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:05.400
However, when Luffy sees Zoro tied in the
courtyard and talks to him, he starts to realize

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.290
that the Marine captain and his son here are
terrible people.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.590
So Luffy being Luffy, I like to think that
he still takes an interest in Zoro and decides

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:18.970
to free him, even if it will cost him his
dream of becoming a Marine.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:24.340
After he beats up Axehand Morgan, he asks
the Marines if he, Koby and Zoro could still

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:29.000
join the Marines, even though he never discussed
it with Zoro.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.870
Now, even though the Marines of the base are
thankful to Luffy, like it happens in the

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:39.820
main story line, when more soldiers arrive
from the Marine headquarters to arrest Morgan,

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.560
he tells them about Luffy’s attack.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:48.500
As a result, the captain of the squad tells
Luffy that even though he is grateful for

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:54.580
what he did, he can’t let someone join the
Marines who attacked a higher up.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:05:00.610
To everyone’s surprise however, Garp is
also on board of the ship, who had come to

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.850
pick up Luffy.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:07.530
And as we know, Garp doesn’t care about
the rules and the higher ups at all and he

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.840
decides to take all of them in as recruits.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.480
So now Luffy, Zoro, Koby and Helmeppo are
making their way towards the grandline and

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:21.350
marine headquarters on board of Garp’s ship,
where he trains all of them hard every single

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.350
day.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:30.360
Remember, Garp was able to teach people like
Koby and Helmeppo a ton of super strong techniques

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:37.389
in a matter of months, so just imagine how
fast Luffy and Zoro would grow under his supervision.

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:42.120
Since Luffy and Zoro are not in need of a
better ship this time tough, they never make

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.800
it to Syrup village, where they meet Usopp
in the main story line.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:52.690
As a result, Captain Kuro can execute his
plan to plunder the village and Usopp is killed.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:56.250
Sanji however is another story.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:01.680
Now, usually Marine ships have a unique ability
that pirate ships don’t.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.991
While all pirates must enter the grand line
by going through reverse mountain, Marine

00:06:05.991 --> 00:06:12.190
ships can actually cross the so-called calm
belt, a strip of ocean between the grand line

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:17.849
and the normal ocean, that has no wind and
is filled with giant sea monsters that sink

00:06:17.849 --> 00:06:21.800
any ship that tries to pass through it.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:27.569
Marine ships use a material called sea stone
that basically makes them invisible to these

00:06:27.569 --> 00:06:33.160
monsters, so they can enter and leave the
grandline when and wherever they please.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:38.090
So Garp could take them directly though the
calm belt to the marine headquarters.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:42.620
But I’d like to think that he would want
to spend as much time with his new recruits

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:49.419
as possible before showing them to the fleet
admiral Sengoku and also show his grandson

00:06:49.419 --> 00:06:50.911
the world a bit.

00:06:50.911 --> 00:06:56.770
So I’m going to assume that Garp would take
the ship towards reverse mountain.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.330
As a result, they would pass by the Baratie
on their way to the grand line.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:05.780
Again this could go either way, because Luffy
really needs to do some convincing to get

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:11.660
Sanji to join his crew, but i like to think
that he would convince Sanji once again to

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.840
see the world with him and look for the all
blue as a marine.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:22.389
Meanwhile, Zoro would still get his duel with
Mihawk, something the other marines are against,

00:07:22.389 --> 00:07:25.490
but Garp allows anyways.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:32.160
Mihawk takes an interest in this marine grunt
who is willing to sacrifice his life for his

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.970
honor as a swordsman.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:38.660
After that, there is of course also a chance
that they never meet Nami and simply pass

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:40.030
by Arlong Park.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:45.600
However, there are two possible reasons why
Garp would take them there anyways.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.040
Maybe he heard about the corrupt Marines in
the area, that Arlong had paid off to leave

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.040
him alone.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.440
Definitely something Garp would do i think.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:59.780
Or maybe Garp knew Bellmere, Nami’s foster
mother, who was a former Marine that found

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:03.250
Nami as a baby and was later killed by Arlong.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.470
After all they were both from the east blue.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:10.010
So he might have decided to visit her grave
on the island.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:18.349
In this case, Luffy, Koby, Helmeppo, Zoro
and Sanji meet Nami and later find her crying.

00:08:18.349 --> 00:08:21.680
Once again Luffy takes them to Arlong Park
and beats him.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:27.520
In memory of her mother Bellmere and in order
to draw a map of the world, Nami decides to

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.379
also join Garp’s squad.

00:08:30.379 --> 00:08:36.330
Luffy is then promoted from Grunt straight
to seaman first class for defeating a powerful

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:41.519
pirate, which would be similar to his 30 million
berry bounty he gets here.

00:08:41.519 --> 00:08:46.839
The last stop before Reverse mountain is Logue
Town, where the group meets Smoker, who immediately

00:08:46.839 --> 00:08:48.899
takes a liking to Luffy.

00:08:48.899 --> 00:08:54.860
Smoker started to like and respect Luffy more
and more in the actual story, despite hating

00:08:54.860 --> 00:09:00.120
pirates, so I think he would vibe really well
with Marine Luffy right from the start.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.870
And while Zoro is looking for new swords to
replace the ones he lost against Mihawk, Luffy

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:10.650
runs into his father Dragon, who is having
a tense conversation with his grandfather.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.190
And then they finally enter the grandline
through reverse mountain.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:21.040
Here they meet Crocus, a member of Gol D.
Roger’s crew, the first pirate king.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.970
He of course knows about Luffy from Shanks.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:28.820
In the main story line, he helps the straw
hats by telling them about the final island

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:35.320
of the grand line Laugh Tale and giving them
the Logue Pose that is necessary to navigate

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:37.029
from island to island.

00:09:37.029 --> 00:09:40.050
In our version however, Crocus is not of too
much help.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:44.220
He greets Garp, because the two of them fought
together against the legendary rocks pirate

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:45.530
crew many years ago.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:50.860
And he tells Garp that Luffy is special and
should have become a pirate.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:54.560
So Luffy doesn’t even know about Laugh Tale
yet here.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:57.800
They group of young Marines also encounters
Vivi.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:05.420
Garp, who knows her father Kobra, the king
of Albasta recognizes her as the princess.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:10.550
Under tears she tells them about Crocodile
and what he has done do her country.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:13.630
Luffy promises her to take her home and help
her.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:18.540
On the way there, they stop at Drum Island,
because Garp has heard rumors about Ace having

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:19.540
been there.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:23.990
Worried for his foster grandson, who is chasing
after Blackbeard, they ask in the village

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.830
if anyone has seen him.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:31.370
Luffy is not able to free Drum island from
Wapol, because he is an official ruler protected

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:37.190
by the world government, but he does get to
meet and recruit chopper.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:43.330
Shortly after that, they reach Alabasta, where
they once again run into smoker to investigate

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.870
what is going on with Crocodile.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:53.250
The warloard laughs at Luffy and Vivi that
they can’t do anything and Luffy prepares

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.500
to fight him.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.850
However Garp steps in to stop Luffy.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:11:01.750
The warloards are part of the world government
and can’t be touched by the Marines.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:07.320
Luffy will have to wait until Garp reports
this to Sengoku and the higher ups.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:13.320
Luffy is starting to get really frustrated
and angry at the Marine system for its unfairness

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:14.730
at this point.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:21.500
Clearly what is happening here is bad, and
he’s supposed to let it go?

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.290
Luffy also quickly meets ace.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:26.170
Then his group runs into Nico Robin.

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:31.630
Garp has no other choice than arresting one
of the most wanted people in the world.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:38.110
When Luffy asks him why, Garp tells him to
be quiet.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:43.950
Leaving Alabasta, they run into Luffy’s
mentor and hero Aokiji, who is biking on the

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:44.950
ocean.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:50.020
Just like in the main timeline, Aokiji came
looking for robin to make sure she was okay.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:55.240
He convinces Garp to not turn her in, but
let her escape.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:12:02.020
This gives him even more points in Luffy’s
book, who then invites Robin to join the Marines.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.459
Garp and Aokiji yell at him that that’s
impossible.

00:12:05.459 --> 00:12:11.060
However a short time later, Robin is being
picked up by the revolutionaries and Dragon,

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.100
although no one knows who contacted him.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:20.529
Since they are on a marine ship, other than
in the main story line, they simply pass by

00:12:20.529 --> 00:12:23.260
Jaya, Water 7 and thriller bark.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:29.130
Franky is at some point caught by CP9, while
Brook is stuck in the florian Triangle for

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:30.490
a bit longer.

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:33.100
However he gets his shadow back a while later.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:38.910
Either when Moria gets defeated at Marineford
or when he tries to attack Kaido in Wano again

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.410
and fails.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:45.589
Instead Luffy’s group manages to capture
some pirates with higher bounties, testing

00:12:45.589 --> 00:12:48.550
out their new skills.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:53.870
Luffy is now already able to use Haki and
also use the techniques of the six powers.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:13:00.070
Before they finally reach Marineford and the
headquarters, they stop at Sabaody archipelago,

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:05.899
where Garp wants to introduce Luffy and the
others to X Drake.

00:13:05.899 --> 00:13:12.860
Drake is one of the few officially known members
of sword and even though Luffy and co don’t

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:18.949
know about it yet, Garp is already planning
to integrate all of them into sword as well.

00:13:18.949 --> 00:13:25.589
On the island Luffy finds his way into the
slave auction house and is absolutely appalled.

00:13:25.589 --> 00:13:30.490
Seeing the celestial dragons reminds him of
the fire at the grey terminal and how the

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.410
celestial dragons sunk Sabo’s ship.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:41.459
luffy is about to punch charlos, just like
in the main time line, when Rayleigh makes

00:13:41.459 --> 00:13:42.470
his appearance.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.709
He knocks out most people in the auction hall
with his conquorers haki and takes Luffy and

00:13:46.709 --> 00:13:48.540
the others to his bar.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:53.270
There he introduces himself as Roger’s right
hand man and tells Luffy that he has been

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.270
waiting for him.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:59.300
He tries to convince Luffy to quit the Marines
and allow him to train with him.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:05.480
Luffy has at this point experienced a number
of heavy blows to his confidence in the marines,

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:13.430
but at that moment Garp comes crashing in
and after a short and heated conversation

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:18.190
with Rayleigh pulls Luffy back to the ship.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:23.959
Finally they arrive at Marineford, where Luffy,
Zoro, Sanji, Nami, Chopper, Koby and Helmeppo

00:14:23.959 --> 00:14:28.520
are all introduced to Sengoku, Kizaru and
Akainu.

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:34.660
Luffy does like Sengoku and seems neutral
towards Kizaru, but it’s clear right from

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:41.930
the start that he already dislikes Akainu
for the way he talks and acts about pirates.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:46.340
The next few weeks, Garp and other officers
train the group hard and send them on a number

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:47.519
of smaller missions.

00:14:47.519 --> 00:14:53.279
Luffy is even promoted to one of the youngest
captains in marine history for his incredible

00:14:53.279 --> 00:14:55.190
fighting ability.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:15:00.380
However then news arrive that his brother
Ace has been captured by Backbeard and handed

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:03.399
over to the government to be executed.

00:15:03.399 --> 00:15:10.829
Luffy snaps at those news and it takes Garp’s
and the squads collective effort to stop Luffy

00:15:10.829 --> 00:15:15.009
marching to impel down by himself to break
Ace out.

00:15:15.009 --> 00:15:19.779
Instead, Marineford starts to prepare for
war against Whitebeard.

00:15:19.779 --> 00:15:24.910
As a result, the prison break from impel down
never happens.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.920
Jinbei doesn’t manage to escape from level
6 either.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:33.199
Most importantly though, without Luffy’s
great escape, Blackbeard’s attempt to recruit

00:15:33.199 --> 00:15:39.510
the level 6 pirates backfires and he and his
crew are defeated by Magellan.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:46.440
The war itself happens quite similarly to
the main timeline, only that Luffy refuses

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.649
to fight at all.

00:15:47.649 --> 00:15:51.149
Now, there are a few different ways this scenario
could go of course.

00:15:51.149 --> 00:15:57.149
One option is that Luffy snaps and joins up
with Whitebeard to try and free Ace anyways.

00:15:57.149 --> 00:16:02.550
We know that Luffy would do anything for his
brother, so it’s not that unlikely he’d

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.550
just throw his marine career aside to do the
right thing.

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:10.730
But for the sake of this story, let’s say
sengoku or someone else stops Luffy from doing

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:14.050
anything when Ace is finally executed.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:16.670
By Akainu of course, for continuity’s sake.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:19.550
Which of course absolutely breaks Luffy.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:26.220
Koby and Shanks stop the war again, but this
time Shanks walks up to Luffy and talks to

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:29.810
him. he tells Luffy that he has the power
to make the world a better place and tells

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:34.430
him to meet him in 2 years in the new world.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:40.470
Only slowly overcoming his pain from loosing
ace, Luffy trains hard for 2 years and finally

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:43.670
Garp invites all of his students to join Sword.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:47.949
Luffy takes the opportunity to meet up with
shanks and joins his crew as an undercover

00:16:47.949 --> 00:16:53.040
agent, like Drake does with Kaido and Aokiji
with blackbeard in the main timeline.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:58.230
Shanks trains luffy even more, teaching him
the truth about his devil fruit, the importance

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:01.430
of finding the one piece and reaching laugh
tale.

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:06.699
And i would say at this point, Luffy either
fully goes back to being a pirate and becoming

00:17:06.699 --> 00:17:13.821
pirate king or he stays a part of sword, reaches
laugh tale and actually manages to become

00:17:13.821 --> 00:17:19.740
the fleet admiral of a marine orginization
that is free and independent of the world

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.319
government.

00:17:21.319 --> 00:17:25.679
I think Luffy is just such a special person,
that even as a marine he would still be able

00:17:25.679 --> 00:17:27.189
to change the world.

00:17:27.189 --> 00:17:31.690
So maybe a much better question to ask, would
be: What would happen to the one piece world

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:35.480
if Luffy was never born in the first place?

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:39.060
Because that one is a lot darker timeline
than this.

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:41.539
If you’re curious you can watch that one
right here.

00:17:41.539 --> 00:17:41.749
THanks for watching.

